# Files that get executed or parsed inside a Linux container must keep LF endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks these out with CRLF. For a shell
# script that turns the shebang into `#!/bin/sh\r`, so the kernel looks for an interpreter named
# literally "/bin/sh\r" and reports the *script* as "not found" -- which sends you looking for a
# missing file that is sitting right there. It cost a debugging session on frontend/
# docker-entrypoint.d/10-tls-fallback.sh, whose image built fine and then had no certificate.
#
# CI never saw it: GitHub Actions checks out on Linux with LF, so only local Windows builds broke.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
